# Block28 no-go discipline

The intended result is constructive: two explicit physical channels.  Any
negative language is bounded by the following checks.

## N1 — alternative routes

Autonomous finite-state history, a targeted `M2` compiler, extensive causal
history, stochastic priority fields, coherent instruments, and action-selected
currents remain live beyond this theorem.

## N2 — wall independence

No general wall is claimed.  The only proposed conclusion is that the listed
effective-carrier conditions do not uniquely fix one joint exit coupling if
two explicit channels pass.

## N3 — hidden walls

Timeouts, memory pressure, cache behavior, and incomplete proofs are excluded
from physics inference.  Conditional Block23/24 status and the supplied input
sector remain visible.

## N4 — residual matching

The readable discriminator must be decoded from the actual new Locked Record
words.  A coefficient difference without Record-level distinguishability is
not enough.

## N5 — rhetoric

Allowed: `two explicit couplings survive the listed scoped constraints`.
Forbidden: `no selector exists`, `Admissibility is inconsistent`, `a new axiom
is required`, or `the Born rule is disproved`.

## N6 — partial closure

Local turn existence, CPTP normalization, covariance, QND action, and readable
odds are individually valuable even if the full theorem fails, but none may
be silently upgraded to autonomous process closure.

## N7 — steelman

A microscopic compiler or autonomous resource/current law may impose an
additional factorization or conservation condition selecting one `lambda`.
That would add physics beyond the tested carrier conditions, not contradict
the scoped construction.

## N8 — cross-cycle echo

Earlier law-underselection examples are route precedent, not proof of this
carrier theorem.  Block28 must stand on its own literal factors and output
Records.

